        <profile name="Abjuror" id="c543-8374-4a2b-fc04" hidden="false" typeId="5156-3fb9-39ce-7bdb" typeName="Operative">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="APL" typeId="bc83-42aa-b7c1-f0b1">2</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Move" typeId="c996-ffb3-e0b4-ecfa">6&quot;</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Save" typeId="3241-5548-12d6-f103">2+</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Wounds" typeId="74f9-f91c-b8fd-89d9">11</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Holy Defender" id="559c-c71d-25d8-164b" hidden="false" typeId="f887-5881-0e6d-755c" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Ability" typeId="3467-0678-083e-eb50">Once per turning point, when a friendly CELESTIAN INSIDIANT operative visible to and within 2&quot; of this operative is selected as the valid target of a **Shoot** action or to fight against during a **Fight** action, you can use this rule. If you do, this operative becomes the valid target or is fought against (as appropriate) instead (even if it wouldn&apos;t normally be valid for this). If it&apos;s the **Fight** action, treat this operative as being within the fighting operative&apos;s control range for the duration of that action. If it&apos;s the **Shoot** action, this operative is only in cover or obscured if the original target was.


This rule has no effect if it&apos;s the **Shoot** action and the ranged weapon has the Blast or Torrent weapon rule.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
